            "review_title": "Review at May Café",
            "review_text": "Paul Strodder\nBridlington, United Kingdom120 contributions\n0\nUpper floor gives a great view of the trains\nJan 2025 • Couples\nWe visited train street in the daytime, and as someone had kindly given us a picture of the train timetable, we were able to book a table upstairs for when the trains were due later in the day. (I have attached the picture which was accurate as of January 2025)\nInexpensive and tasty food which was freshly cooked to order. The owner was friendly and helpful and the other staff were quick to respond to the bell for you to call for service as you can’t be seen by the staff when you sit upstairs.\nDepending on how you want to see the trains come through, you can of course sit downstairs, but we enjoyed the experience from the upper floor.\nThere are many restaurants and bars along train street, so your choice is quite good, and we sat at another one a bit up the track for a drink and snack the previous day, either way, the experience is worth doing as it is pretty unique.\nRead more\nWritten January 14, 2025",
